language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session3_people_in_a_room: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ There are 13 people, 4 of them male. They enter a room one at a time, in some order. Find an order of entry in which the males and females enter so that the ratio of females to males in the room is no greater than 7/3 at any one time.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session3_people_in_a_room.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ n: the number of people
letting n = 13
$ males: the number of male people
letting males = 4
$ females: the number of female people, the rest of the n people
letting females = n - males

$ sequence[i]: the i-th person to enter the room is female (true) or male (false)
find sequence : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool
$ females_in[k]: auxiliary, the number of females among the first k people to enter
find females_in : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..n)

branching on [sequence]

such that
$ all the people enter: exactly the females (9 of the 13) are marked true
(sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(sequence[i])) = females,
$ females_in[k] counts the females among the first k entrants
forAll k : int(1..n) . females_in[k] = (sum i : int(1..k) . toInt(sequence[i])),
$ at every point the females in the room are at most 7/3 of the males, so 3 times the females is at most 7 times the males, where the males in the room are the k entrants less the females
forAll k : int(1..n) . 3 * females_in[k] <= 7 * (k - females_in[k])
